But what it was like for you to kind of like, meet that character on the page, before you met me or Carter or Pam or anything else, like you see this on the page, you know you're gonna come in audition for it.
但对你来说，在见到我、卡特、帕姆或其他任何人之前，在剧本上初次遇到那个角色是什么感觉？就像你在剧本上看到这个，你知道你要来试镜。

00:09:27.220 --> 00:09:32.259
Remember our casting director, Megan Brandman was like, this is somebody really interesting.
还记得我们的选角导演梅根·布兰德曼当时说，这是一个非常有趣的人。

00:09:32.259 --> 00:09:40.539
This is somebody you're gonna take really seriously for this role, and I give her a lot of credit, Megan, for really perking us up to pay attention here.
这是一个你会为这个角色认真对待的人，我非常感谢梅根，是他提醒了我们要特别关注这一点。

00:09:40.539 --> 00:09:45.340
This is somebody special, you were very young, you had not done any comedy, I don't think, right?
这是一个特别的人，你当时很年轻，我记得你之前没演过喜剧吧？

00:09:45.340 --> 00:09:46.940
You had been on some hour shows?
你之前演过一些一小时时长的剧集？

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:55.460
I'm just curious to hear your perspective of finding that script, coming in that audition, meeting that character, meeting us, and kind of where, what that felt like from your perspective.
我很好奇想听听你的视角：发现那个剧本、来参加试镜、遇到那个角色、遇到我们，从你的角度来看，那是一种什么样的感觉。

00:09:55.460 --> 00:10:02.460
We talked about that with Joshua, he came in, he remembered the office, he came in an audition which I think it was the same one you came in, but what do you remember of that?
我们和约书亚聊过这个，他来了，他记得那个办公室，他来试镜——我想跟你们来的是同一个，但你对那有什么记忆？

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:05.307
Pan as little word picture there.
帕姆在那用语言描绘了一幅画。

00:10:05.307 --> 00:10:07.033
Yeah, let's go back.
好吧，我们回想一下。

00:10:07.033 --> 00:10:10.139
So I was and still am very Canadian.
所以我当时是，现在也依然非常加拿大。

00:10:10.139 --> 00:10:11.659
I think I'm still 23.
我觉得我好像还是23岁。

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:24.202
So I was living in Canada and we would do this sort of Canadian migration every year because there was a pilot season.
所以当时我住在加拿大，我们每年都会进行这种所谓的加拿大候鸟式迁徙，因为当时有试播集季。

00:10:24.202 --> 00:10:30.543
And so you would, I would, you know, I worked in restaurants all year and I saved up money.
所以你会，我会，你知道的，我整年都在餐馆打工攒钱。

00:10:30.543 --> 00:10:35.073
And then I drove my Volkswagen Jetta, Sadie, Mashi Rest in Peace.
然后我开着我的大众捷达，萨迪，马希，愿她安息。

00:10:35.073 --> 00:10:36.815
Sadie, I never knew this.
萨迪，我从来不知道这件事。

00:10:36.815 --> 00:10:38.905
See, we're breaking news here.
看，我们这有独家新闻。

00:10:38.905 --> 00:10:39.405
Sadie.
萨迪。

00:10:39.405 --> 00:10:40.869
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

00:10:40.869 --> 00:10:43.029
Everyone's know my first heart.
每个人都知道我的初恋。

00:10:43.029 --> 00:10:47.767
You can't imagine the amount of you or male we've gotten about this.
你无法想象我们收到了多少关于这件事的粉丝邮件。

00:10:47.767 --> 00:10:49.021
So we're thrilled.
所以我们太兴奋了。

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:52.500
It's mostly the answer, the top question.
这基本上是大家问得最多的问题。

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:54.100
Thanks for being with us, Kobe.
谢谢你和我们在一起，科比。

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:56.139
This was so wonderful.
这太棒了。

00:10:56.139 --> 00:10:56.820
I was right.
我猜得没错。

00:10:56.820 --> 00:11:00.370
You guys are so nice to see everyone.
你们见到大家真好。

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:09.690
No, me and Sadie Lady, we drove down and, you know, I lived with two of my best friends in Venice when it was not nice.
不，我和萨迪小姐，我们开车南下，你知道的，我和我最好的两个朋友住在威尼斯海滩，当时那里还不是什么好地方。

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:12.769
Venice, Abbot Kinney when it was not fancy.
威尼斯，阿伯特金尼大道，当时还很不高级的时候。

00:11:12.769 --> 00:11:17.250
And, you know, we just auditioned like crazy.
你知道的，我们就是疯狂地去试镜。

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:23.450
you would do, you know, if you were lucky, you would get multiple auditions a week a day.
如果你幸运的话，你一周甚至一天会得到好几次试镜机会。

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:24.769
And it was kind of madness.
那简直有点疯狂。

00:11:24.769 --> 00:11:33.929
It was kind of like a, you know, this fever dream of, you know, getting eight pages of sides to memorize for the next day.
这就像是一种狂热的梦境，要为第二天背诵八页的台词。

00:11:33.929 --> 00:11:42.169
And just hoping that something would click and then, you know, networks were making multiple pilots every year.
然后只是祈祷能有哪个角色合适，然后，你知道的，电视台每年都在制作好几个试播集。

00:11:42.169 --> 00:11:44.889
So you would kind of go like, okay, I'll get a pilot maybe.
所以你大概会想，好吧，我可能会拿到一个试播集。

00:11:44.889 --> 00:11:53.370
and then I'll at least, you know, and for me being a Canadian, being an immigrant, I was like, please God, get me a job down here so I can stay.
然后我至少能……对我来说，作为加拿大人，作为一个移民，我就在想：求求上帝，让我在南方找个工作吧，这样我才能留下来。

00:11:53.370 --> 00:12:23.230
So I came down, I drove down, and I was auditioning for multiple pilots, and I think I was set to test for something, which I can't remember, but I do think that Mark Paul Glosser, who was who played Zach Morris, was in this other pilot, so I was really excited because I didn't very much in love with him for a majority of my teenage life.
所以我南下了，我开车过来，我为好几个试播集试镜，我想我当时准备为某个剧试镜，我不记得是什么了，但我确实觉得马克-保罗·戈塞拉——也就是扮演扎克·莫里斯的那个人——也在另一个试播集中，所以我当时非常兴奋，因为在我的青少年时期大部分时间里，我都非常迷恋他。

00:12:23.230 --> 00:12:25.830
Wait, a pilot against, at the same time as the average mother pilot isn't?
等等，一个试播集对立着——与此同时《老爸老妈浪漫史》的试播集不是吗？

00:12:25.830 --> 00:12:46.350
Yeah, before I had even met you, I had auditioned for this, Zach Morris, we're not gonna call him that, but like, I'm sorry, that's like, like, of Mark, okay, we'll call him Mark by his actual name, Mark, and to play his sister, and I was like, this is confusing because I'm very much in love with, like, I spent a majority of my teen years, very much in love with this human.
对，甚至在我遇到你之前，我曾为这个试播集试镜，扎克·莫里斯，我们不这么叫他，但就像是，对不起，那就是——马克，好吧，我们用他的真名叫他马克，去演他的妹妹，我就觉得这很让人困惑，因为我非常迷恋，我度过了大部分青少年时期，都非常迷恋这个人类。

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:55.049
So I was set, they were doing sort of, I think, Josh, you sort of spoke to everybody about the testing process.
所以我当时准备好了，他们正在进行某种——我想，约什你跟大家都聊过试播测试的过程。

00:12:55.049 --> 00:12:58.450
So I won't bore everybody with like network studio and all that stuff.
所以我不会用电视台、制片厂以及所有那些事情来烦大家了。

00:12:58.450 --> 00:13:08.970
But I was set to test with him and then got a call from Megan and stuff and went in and read.
但我当时准备和马克一起测试，然后接到了梅根的电话，然后就去读了剧本。

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:11.889
And then I said, you know, I'm testing for this other show.
然后我说，你知道的，我正在为另一部剧做测试。

00:13:11.889 --> 00:13:16.190
And then I think like that she brought me in like the next day to meet with you guys.
然后我想她第二天就把我叫来跟你们见面了。

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:17.029
Oh my God.
天哪。

00:13:17.029 --> 00:13:18.129
I don't think I ever knew this.
我想我以前从来不知道这件事。

00:13:18.129 --> 00:13:19.889
I'm feeling this weird emotion.
我有一种奇怪的情绪。

00:13:19.889 --> 00:13:23.370
Like I'm slightly jealous of Mark Paul, Goss, I don't know where it's going to be.
就像我有点嫉妒马克·保罗·戈斯，我不知道这会走向何方。

00:13:23.370 --> 00:13:26.809
I'm like, get away from Kobe.
我就想：离科比远点！

00:13:26.809 --> 00:13:27.769
She's going to be our Robin.
她会是我们的罗宾。

00:13:27.769 --> 00:13:29.210
I'm like having a whole time travel thing.
我感觉自己像是在经历一次时空旅行。

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:30.049
No, yes.
不，是的。

00:13:30.049 --> 00:13:30.889
That's hilarious.
这太搞笑了。

00:13:30.889 --> 00:13:32.009
She was sort of fast-tracked to me.
她基本上是被快速引荐给我的。

00:13:32.009 --> 00:13:35.330
And she was like, okay, we'll come in tomorrow and you can meet Kari and Craig.
她说，好吧，你明天来，可以见见卡里和克雷格。

00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:36.850
And I was like, we're right.
我就想：好的。

00:13:36.850 --> 00:13:47.649
And so I met you guys and immediately, like to felt like this is really funny, but as you had said, Greg, I had never done a comedy.
于是我见到了你们，立刻就觉得这真的很有趣，但正如你所说的那样，克雷格，我从来没有演过喜剧。

00:13:47.649 --> 00:13:54.570
I've done sort of hour long dramas, mostly up in Canada.
我以前在加拿大演过大约一小时时长的正剧。

00:13:54.570 --> 00:13:58.289
And so I was not sure if I was funny.
所以我并不确定自己是否有幽默感。

00:13:58.289 --> 00:14:07.639
I mean, I think I could make friends and family laugh, but it was a different, it was a different rhythm And it was a different sort of demand.
我的意思是，我觉得我能让朋友和家人笑，但那是完全不同的节奏，也是完全不同的要求。

00:14:07.639 --> 00:14:12.639
And so I tried my best, and I guess I fooled ya.
所以我尽力了，我想我骗过你们了。

00:14:16.139 --> 00:14:17.779
I fooled ya.
我骗过你们了。

00:14:17.779 --> 00:14:20.620
And only for nine years though.
不过只骗了九年。

00:14:20.620 --> 00:14:22.559
So you really didn't do a good job.
所以你其实也没做好。

00:14:22.559 --> 00:14:23.559
Good.
很好。

00:14:23.559 --> 00:14:25.519
I don't know when you're gonna pull the plug out.
我不知道你什么时候会拔掉插头。

00:14:25.519 --> 00:14:26.519
It's still working.
它仍然在运作。

00:14:26.519 --> 00:14:28.559
I still think you're funny.
我还是觉得你很有趣。

00:14:28.559 --> 00:14:31.039
Yeah, and then it was sort of a similar process.
是的，然后这是一个类似的过程。

00:14:31.039 --> 00:14:38.080
I remember meeting Josh, but we were lucky enough to do the studio network test together.
我记得见过约什，但我们很幸运能一起参加制片厂和电视台的测试。

00:14:38.159 --> 00:14:42.000
And it felt very, it felt very lovely and very easy.
感觉非常可爱，也非常轻松。

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:47.720
And it was, I think probably the best version of that process can be.
这可以说是那个流程中最完美的形式了。

00:14:47.720 --> 00:14:53.519
I felt very, when I read the script for the first time, I just, I fell in love.
当我第一次读到这个剧本时，我真的坠入爱河了。

00:14:53.519 --> 00:14:59.480
I mean, Robin isn't in the pilot very much if I'm, like she's sort of, it's more about this group of people.
我的意思是，如果我没记错的话，罗宾在试播集里戏份并不多，她差不多是……这集更多是关于这一群人的。

00:14:59.480 --> 00:15:06.229
And I remember being like, oh gosh, hope I can stay and become a part of this group.
我记得当时在想：哦天哪，希望我能留下来，成为这群人中的一员。

00:15:06.229 --> 00:15:12.737
But I thought she was, and even in the opening, people saying she's so confident.
但我觉得她，甚至在一开始，大家就说她太自信了。

00:15:12.737 --> 00:15:15.549
And I didn't feel like that at all.
而我一点也没有那种感觉。

00:15:15.549 --> 00:15:17.789
I was very much acting.
我完全是在演。

00:15:17.789 --> 00:15:27.823
Well, what's funny is the plot of the first two episodes of How Much Mother is this young woman from Canada hopes she can come to America and become part of this friend group.
有趣的是，《老爸老妈浪漫史》前两集的剧情就是这个来自加拿大的年轻女性希望她能来到美国并成为这个朋友圈的一部分。

00:15:27.823 --> 00:15:33.269
And you actually it felt exactly the way that was what the character felt and what you thought.
而你当时的感觉完全就是那个角色所感受到的，也是你当时所想的。

00:15:33.269 --> 00:15:36.269
But to be fair, she was not Canadian yet.
但公平地说，她当时还不是加拿大人。

00:15:36.269 --> 00:15:37.110
You made her Canadian.
你们把她设定成了加拿大人。

00:15:37.110 --> 00:15:37.950
No, it's true.
不，确实如此。

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:38.789
We didn't.
我们没有。

00:15:38.789 --> 00:15:40.509
We made her Canadian in honor of you.
我们为了向你致敬，才把她设定为加拿大人。

00:15:40.509 --> 00:15:41.350
That's true.
没错。

00:15:41.350 --> 00:15:55.750
You know, I do sometimes think that when you get a role that is kind of like a role that kind of becomes iconic, like our roles all became, there is something about that it feels bigger than just, oh, you were right for the part.
你知道，有时我确实认为，当你得到一个某种程度上会成为标志性的角色时——就像我们所有的角色最终都成为的那样，这里面有些东西感觉比单纯的“你很适合这个角色”要宏大得多。

00:15:55.750 --> 00:15:58.190
Like it feels like your DNA was right for the part.
就好像你的基因天生就适合这个角色一样。

00:15:58.190 --> 00:16:02.269
like there's a mystical thing that happens.
就像有什么神秘的事情在发生。

00:16:02.269 --> 00:16:13.470
And even as Craig lays it out, it's like, yeah, you were acting, you were doing these things, but you were also like, where you were in your life on the earth at that moment, was exactly what was required for the show.
即使在克雷格（Craig）剖析之后，也会觉得，是的，你在演戏，你在做这些事情，但同时，你当时在人生的那个阶段、在地球上所处的位置，恰好就是这部剧所需要的。

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:19.470
And where I was in my life thing was exactly what was needed in the show.
我当时在人生中的状态，恰好就是这部剧所需要的。

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:23.669
So it's almost like, yes, acting's hard landing jokes is challenging and all that.
所以这几乎就像是，是的，演戏很难，抖包袱很有挑战性，诸如此类。

00:16:23.669 --> 00:16:25.789
You're technically doing things.
你在技术上确实在做这些事情。

00:16:25.789 --> 00:16:29.129
But there's also something where you're like, You can't actually screw it up.
但某种程度上，你会觉得，你其实根本不会搞砸。

00:16:29.129 --> 00:16:34.070
If you're that right for the role, you're just going to be the person, you know?
如果你和这个角色如此契合，你自然就会成为那个人，你知道吗？

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:35.070
And you were.
而你确实就是。

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:36.070
And that's the thing.
这就是关键所在。

00:16:36.070 --> 00:16:38.789
We never wanted anybody else for the part once we saw you.
一旦我们见到了你，我们就再没想过让其他人来演这个角色。

00:16:38.789 --> 00:16:43.309
It was just how do we convince a network that is going to say, what else has she done in terms of comedy?
问题只在于，我们该如何说服电视网，他们肯定会问：“她在喜剧方面还演过什么？”

00:16:43.309 --> 00:16:44.309
What's her real?
“她的真实水平是什么？”

00:16:44.309 --> 00:16:45.309
Where are all her clips?
“她的喜剧片段都在哪儿？”

00:16:45.309 --> 00:16:50.610
And we had to make the point in this show, it's a character meeting this woman out of nowhere.
而我们必须在这部剧中指出这一点：这是一个角色在酒吧里偶遇一个突如其来的女人。

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:53.669
And wouldn't it be nice for America to also be meeting this woman?
那让全美观众也偶遇这样一位女性，不是也挺好的吗？

00:16:53.669 --> 00:16:55.110
They've never seen on other sitcoms.
他们从未在其他情景喜剧中见过她。

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:56.990
She hasn't done 12 other sitcoms.
她没有拍过另外12部情景喜剧。

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:59.110
this is her first one and that's a good thing.
这是她的第一部，而这绝对是件好事。

00:16:59.110 --> 00:16:59.950
And they got it.
他们理解了。

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:00.789
So they're credit.
所以这要归功于他们。

00:17:00.789 --> 00:17:01.629
Then I work in the studio.
后来我在制片厂工作。

00:17:01.629 --> 00:17:02.950
They got, they got that that's Ted.
他们懂了，他们明白泰德（Ted）当时在吧台对面遇到了她，全美观众也是如此，这感觉就像是命中注定。

00:17:02.950 --> 00:17:08.430
Ted was meeting her in that moment across the bar and so was America and it felt meant to be.
真的就是这样。

00:17:08.430 --> 00:17:09.269
It really did.
真的如此。

00:17:09.269 --> 00:17:17.470
I think it's also, I hear you Josh, but I think it's also like the credit goes to you and Carter as well.
我也觉得，乔治（Josh），我听到你的话了，但我认为荣誉也应该归功于你和卡特（Carter）。

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:24.109
And also I will say Pam Fryman, like there was this sort of very safe environment.
而且我还要感谢帕姆·弗莱曼（Pam Fryman），当时有一种非常安全的环境。

00:17:24.109 --> 00:17:25.000
environment.
环境。

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:32.199
You know, the credit also would go to the studio CBS and Fox because they didn't notice to death.
你知道，荣誉也应该归功于CBS电视台和福克斯制片厂，因为他们没有对我们进行过度干涉。

00:17:32.199 --> 00:17:40.289
So when we're taping and we're recording all these things, first of all, you're surrounded by amazing actors.
所以当我们拍摄和录制所有这些内容时，首先，你的周围都是优秀的演员。

00:17:40.289 --> 00:17:49.789
You have Pam Fryman, who's like mother to, I mean, for me, and I think a lot of other people on that set would say that as well.
你有帕姆·弗莱曼，她就像是大家的母亲，我是说，对我而言，我想片场的许多其他人也会这样说。

00:17:49.789 --> 00:18:03.484
you know, it created this especially for someone like me who was quite terrified and really sort of working with these other actors who were so funny and so talented and had done so much more than I had.
你知道，这创造了一种氛围，尤其是对于像我这样感到十分恐惧、而且真的需要和这些其他演员合作的人来说，他们是如此风趣、如此才华横溢，而且比我经验丰富得多。

00:18:03.484 --> 00:18:15.425
I felt a lot of pressure and it was this wonderful environment to step into to be like, yeah, you can totally bomb and then we'll just do another take and then it'll get better.
我感到了巨大的压力，但能走进这样一个美妙的环境，听到“没关系，你完全可以演砸，然后我们再拍一条，就会变得更好”，这种感觉真好。

00:18:15.425 --> 00:18:24.532
