01:09:04.920 --> 01:09:36.666
She sort of creates an endeavor that can be a place, not a school, but it's a place where her young adult son with Down Syndrome can work, it's this coffee shop, which is also based on some amazing people I know in the Berkshires, I'm gonna give them a shout out that they created this coffee shop for their child with a disability or young adult with a disability, and they create a coffee shop called Extra Specialties that has two locations in the Berkshires, and just getting to know them bit and seeing what they did with that kind of informed one of the character's journeys the mother who literally does that, essentially in my book.
她可以说是开创了一项事业，那不是一所学校，而是一个地方——她患有唐氏综合征的成年儿子可以在那里工作，是一家咖啡馆。这也是以我在伯克希尔认识的一些了不起的人为原型的，我要向他们致敬，他们为自己的残障孩子或患有残障的年轻成年人创办了这家咖啡馆，他们创办了一家名为“特别特产”（Extra Specialties）的咖啡馆，在伯克希尔有两个分店。稍微了解他们一下，看看他们所做的事情，为我书中某个人物的旅程提供了灵感，也就是那位在书中基本上亲历了这一切的母亲。

01:09:36.666 --> 01:09:42.767
So yeah, Elliot, my son, the experience of raising him is in the book, but just the osmosis of all of these amazing people.
所以，是的，我儿子埃利奥特的抚养经历融入了书中，同时还有所有这些了不起的人带来的潜移默化的影响。

01:09:42.767 --> 01:09:49.662
When you have a child with a disability, at first you feel so alone and you feel so overwhelmed, you don't know how you can possibly do it.
当你拥有一个残障孩子时，起初你会感到无比孤独，不知所措，不知道自己到底该怎么熬过去。

01:09:49.662 --> 01:10:03.800
And then you realize one of the answers to that question, how can you possibly get through this and do this and know how to do it is you just get to absorb all of this amazing wisdom and positivity and creativity from all of these other people you meet within the disability community.
然后你会意识到，对于“你究竟怎么才能熬过去、挺过来并找到方法”这个问题，其中一个答案就是：你只需去汲取残障群体中你遇到的所有其他人的惊人智慧、积极心态和创造力。

01:10:03.800 --> 01:10:09.920
So I tried to put all of that in the book, the parts that are about Elliot and the parts that are just me being inspired by other people.
所以我试图把所有这些都写进书里，既有关于埃利奥特的部分，也有受其他人启发的部分。

01:10:09.920 --> 01:10:12.600
And there's also an element of Hollywood in the book.
书里还有一个好莱坞的元素。

01:10:12.600 --> 01:10:19.119
It's the plot of the book is that there's a movie being made about the life story of this family.
书的情节是：有人正在把这个家庭的生活故事拍成电影。

01:10:19.119 --> 01:10:26.552
So I have fun with sort of the Hollywood part of my life and I have fun with the disability parenthood part of my life.
所以我把生活中的好莱坞部分写得很有趣，把身为残障儿童父母的部分也写得很有趣。

01:10:26.552 --> 01:10:34.172
I sort of bought these two huge worlds that have been essentially my entire adult life and put them together in this book.
我基本上把这两个几乎占据了我整个成年生活的大世界结合在了一起，写进了这本书里。

01:10:34.172 --> 01:10:38.731
And it's a comedy, but I hope it's poignant and I'll stop selling it now.
这是一部喜剧，但我希望它感人至深，我不宣传了。

01:10:38.731 --> 01:10:42.229
What was the Simpsons where the production came to town?
那是《辛普森一家》里的哪一集，摄制组来到小镇的那集？

01:10:42.229 --> 01:10:49.349
And they say like, we're just simple folk from Hollywood and these small town grifters took us for all were worse.
他们说：“我们只是来自好莱坞的单纯乡下人，结果却被这些小镇骗子把我们的钱全骗光了。”

01:10:49.349 --> 01:10:52.159
We just wanted to tell a story, a pure story.
“我们只想讲一个故事，一个纯粹的故事。”

01:10:52.159 --> 01:10:53.159
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

01:10:53.159 --> 01:10:54.159
Yeah.
对。

01:10:54.159 --> 01:10:55.159
I love that about the school.
我很喜欢学校的这一点。

01:10:55.159 --> 01:11:03.000
It reminds me of something they say in 12 steps that someone told me that if you're not hearing at a meeting what you need to hear, you have to be the one to share it.
这让我想起他们在戒酒互助会（12步项目）里说的一句话，有人曾告诉我：如果在会上没有听到你想听的话，你就必须成为那个分享它的人。

01:11:03.000 --> 01:11:04.000
Right.
没错。

01:11:04.000 --> 01:11:05.000
Right.
没错。

01:11:05.000 --> 01:11:09.159
And it's just kind of like, if it doesn't exist and you need it in the world, like make it.
这就好比是，如果它不存在而世界又需要它，那就自己创造它。

01:11:09.159 --> 01:11:10.159
Yeah.
对。

01:11:10.159 --> 01:11:11.159
Like, that's almost the thing.
就像是那种感觉。

01:11:11.159 --> 01:11:21.520
Like, um, there's that quote, is it a Howard Thurman quote, or he says, find out where your your deep hunger and the world, no, where your deep joy and the world's deep hunger meet.
就像，嗯，有句名言，是霍华德·瑟曼（Howard Thurman）的名言吗？他说，找出你内心的饥渴与世界的，不对，是找出你内心的快乐与世界深切的饥渴相契合的地方。

01:11:21.520 --> 01:11:22.520
Right.
对吧？

01:11:22.520 --> 01:11:23.520
Yes.
对。

01:11:23.520 --> 01:11:24.520
Yes.
没错。

01:11:24.520 --> 01:11:25.520
Yes.
完全正确。

01:11:25.520 --> 01:11:26.520
Absolutely.
绝对是的。

01:11:26.520 --> 01:11:28.880
Like this sounds like a book that you would have loved to have read when Elliot was young.
这听起来像是一本你在埃利奥特小时候会很想读的书。

01:11:28.880 --> 01:11:36.600
This is a book I would have loved to have read the day after my son got his diagnosis of having a rare genetic syndrome.
这本书正是我在我儿子被诊断出患有罕见遗传综合征的第二天，做梦都想读到的书。

01:11:36.600 --> 01:11:39.760
But I also hope that it's a book that will speak to every family anywhere.
但我也希望它是一本能触动任何地方、每一个家庭的书。

01:11:39.760 --> 01:11:44.720
It's really a comedic novel about a family and there happens to be this disability piece in it too.
这其实是一部关于一个家庭的喜剧小说，其中恰好包含了一部分残障元素。

01:11:44.720 --> 01:11:47.566
happens to be this piece that there's a movie being made about them.
恰好也有人把他们的故事拍成电影的桥段。

01:11:47.566 --> 01:11:52.800
But essentially I, the book, the book will only have been a success if it speaks to every family and every person everywhere.
但本质上，这本书只有在它能触动到世界各地每一个家庭和每一个人的时候，才算真正取得了成功。

01:11:52.800 --> 01:11:54.840
So I hope that's what it does.
所以我希望它能做到这一点。

01:11:54.840 --> 01:11:55.860
It's all order.
这要求很高。

01:11:55.860 --> 01:11:57.289
But that was my goal.
但这就是我的目标。

01:11:57.289 --> 01:12:00.554
I'm sure the internet will tell me all the kids.
我相信网友们会把我的缺点全挑出来的。

01:12:00.554 --> 01:12:05.519
Can we also plug that we're supporting research from Dr. Paul Grossfield?
我们能顺便宣传一下我们在支持保罗·格罗斯菲尔德（Paul Grossfield）医生的研究吗？

01:12:05.520 --> 01:12:06.020
Yeah.
可以。

01:12:06.020 --> 01:12:06.520
Yeah.
对。

01:12:06.520 --> 01:12:21.874
Dr. Paul Grossfeld, he's he is the doctor who specializes in my son's condition, Jacobson syndrome, but he works to help all kids with congenital heart issues and sort of has a subspecialty in my son's sort of branch of having congenital heart issues and other things with this rare syndrome.
保罗·格罗斯菲尔德医生，他是专门研究我儿子病情——雅各布森综合征的医生，但他致力于帮助所有患有先天性心脏病的儿童，并且在治疗我儿子所患的那类罕见综合征引起的先天性心脏病及其他问题方面有着细分专长。

01:12:21.399 --> 01:12:27.840
But he's a pediatric cardiologist and we were raising money to support his lab and his research on the podcast.
但他是一位小会儿心脏病专家，我们在播客中筹集资金来支持他的实验室和研究。

